+/**
+ * Tell the parser about the document's root element (VitaSurf).
+ *
+ * Custom properties are substituted as the sheet is parsed, long before
+ * any element exists, so a --name declaration is only collected when its
+ * selector can be recognised as addressing the root. Sites do not write
+ * their palettes on a bare :root: they hang them off an attribute or a
+ * class on <html> and switch theme by changing it, and github.com ships
+ * sixteen mutually exclusive blocks of 959 colours each, with no
+ * unconditional fallback. Without knowing which one applies, every
+ * colour on the page resolves to nothing.
